n":{"commit_sha":"047970c8ed5c06985a04774b73280b19321c73a8","position":"1787376261692816001-4842a04d-30f0-45a6-b4e2-96568a816641"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-239_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"e50ec61e-3a77-4eb8-b56b-c1d0f90ff9bc","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed as Gerrit 2057 (commit 75d8c2526b). Held-out TDD: 8 tests authored, implementer saw only 2 happy-path; RED baseline 7 RED / 1 pinning-green (the _CASCADING_EDGES table test, correctly green before and after). Two mutations killed by their exact held-out tests: removing the benign-race TOCTOU re-check killed test_a_benign_parent_race_still_lets_the_child_proceed; removing the cycle guard killed test_a_malformed_parent_cycle_terminates. Gates: lint rc=0, mypy 626 files clean, complexity new=0 increased=0 with claim_compute and _cascade_parent_first both going STALE (i.e. simpler), 48 tests green including all 32 in test_claim_transition_parent_cascade.py and all 7 in test_inbound_status_cascade.py with zero assertion edits. CONVERGENCE RECORDED per the parent epic's clause: the two call sites previously raised differently worded failures ('cannot claim X: claiming its parent Y failed first' vs 'cannot move X to Z: transitioning its parent Y to Z failed first'); a single verb-parameterised message cannot reproduce both, so they now share one wording. No test asserts that text; docs/concurrency.md:117 quoted the old claim phrasing and was updated. Exit codes and the ConcurrencyMismatch re-raise are unchanged. apply_inbound_events was deliberately left alone: it already single-sources the DECISION, and its walk returns written event paths topmost-first, an ordering its own suite pins that the shared recursive helper cannot reproduce without complicating the signature.","timestamp":1787369764995346001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"LANDED: Gerrit 2057 submitted, merged as b46a901937 on main, after LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1. The first Verified was -1 from tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_ensures.py::test_mcp_startup_sweeps_before_run, a KNOWN order-dependent flake (open bug de95-1594-1056-436e) provably disjoint from this change; rechecked with that reasoning stated, and the flake itself is being root-caused under its own ticket rather than retried. AC EVIDENCE: 9 acceptance criteria all verified. AC1's command as originally written could never pass - '_CASCADING_EDGES\\\\s*=' does not match a definition that carries a type annotation between the name and the '=', and \\\\s is not basic regex; corrected to 'grep -rnE \"^_CASCADING_EDGES\"', which returns exactly one definition at transition.py:415 with 9 references. All three cascading edges verified by the 32-test suite passing unchanged; the inbound cascade from Gerrit 2044 keeps its own write primitive and topmost-first ordering (7 tests, apply_inbound_events.py untouched - 0 files matched in the landed diff); '* -> closed' still does not cascade; both cascade=False suppression tests pass. reopen was confirmed to already cascade via the (closed -> open) row, answering the open question this ticket posed. Also landed: the review bot's advisory that the unified error message read awkwardly was FIXED rather than deferred - a single verb could not render naturally in both slots ('cannot move to in_progress X', 'its parent could not claim'), so the API now takes an action phrase plus a past participle.","timestamp":1787374729009346001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Description condensed for the plan-review close gate. During implementation two long sections ('Companion-ticket status, corrected' and 'Code-reading corrections') were appended to the DESCRIPTION, taking it from 4392 to 8980 chars. That made the close gate report stale-material, and a re-review was not possible either: 8980 chars is over the 8000-char plan-review admission cap (criterion P4), so review-plan would have blocked it unread. The description is now 6412 chars and retains all the substance - Context, Approach (including why the decision table is NOT moved and why apply_inbound_events stays separate), Guard construction, Scope, Testing, a compressed 5-point corrections summary, and all 9 acceptance criteria with their existing ticks. Nothing was dropped that changes the plan; the FULL code-reading corrections, the Gerrit 2044 companion-ticket detail, and the landed AC evidence remain verbatim in the two earlier comments on this ticket, which are immutable. Re-running review-plan now against the condensed text.","timestamp":1787376261692816001}],"created_at":1787352180718047001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"80aa6b78-0e17-42cd-8cfd-f5a7da43a7f5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0446-4278-b7df-438d"},{"link_uuid":"8e9db52f-a659-43af-ada9-ff9443c6782c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"bb73-97de-eeea-4899"},{"link_uuid":"ea45bb57-c45f-4b36-bb9a-b91c3d12fd6c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3939-c860-0637-46af"},{"link_uuid":"6b86c0bf-2be2-457d-9464-2eaf08aee984","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5b13-b5a5-6b88-4772"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe parent-first cascade is implemented twice: `src/rebar/_commands/claim.py:200-237` (hardcodes\nthe `open` parent via `_resolve_open_parent`) and `src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:421-493`\n(`_cascade_parent_first`, driven by the `_CASCADING_EDGES` table at `transition.py:414`). The\ntable was added after bug `cranial-sulfur-peafowl` and extended again for\n`paragonite-fruited-minnow` — both were \"an edge the cascade did not know about\" — and the claim\ncopy still cannot express any edge but `open→in_progress`. The ghost/init preconditions at\n`transition.py:308-323` and `claim.py:156-169` are byte-identical. Open task\n`convenient-unrational-songbird` covers the table's one-status-per-edge shape; this story is the\nsingle implementation it then builds on.\n\n## Approach\nAdd `src/rebar/_commands/lifecycle_cascade.py` with\n\n    cascade_parent_first(ticket_id, *, eligible_status, resolve_parent, advance,\n                         action, parent_action, cascade_seen=None) -> None\n\nextracting **the walk only**: the ancestor recursion, the cycle guard, the benign-race TOCTOU\nre-check, and the error rewrap that preserves `ConcurrencyMismatch` (and therefore exit 10) at\nthe leaf. `resolve_parent` and `advance` are injected, so each caller keeps its own WRITE\nPRIMITIVE — the only thing that genuinely differs between the sites.\n\n**The decision table is NOT moved.** `_CASCADING_EDGES` stays at `transition.py:415`, and\n`transition._cascade_parent_first` keeps its name, signature and `cascade` guard, delegating only\nthe walk. This is deliberate: the inbound writer from Gerrit 2044 ALREADY single-sources the\ndecision by importing `_CASCADING_EDGES` and `_resolve_parent_in_status`, so there is no second\ncopy of the decision to unify — only the walk is duplicated.\n\n`claim_compute` passes `eligible_status=\"open\"` with an `advance` closure recursing into\n`claim_compute`; `transition._cascade_parent_first` passes the edge's eligible status with an\n`advance` closure recursing into `transition_compute`. `action`/`parent_action` are two strings\nrather than one verb because no single word renders naturally in both message slots.\n\n`apply_inbound_events._cascade_inbound_status_parents` is deliberately NOT rewired: its walk\nreturns the written event paths topmost-first, an ordering its own suite pins, which a recursive\nhelper returning `None` cannot reproduce without complicating the signature for the two callers\nthat do not need it.\n\nGuard: `_CASCADING_EDGES` is defined exactly once under `src/rebar`\n(`grep -rnE \"^_CASCADING_EDGES\" src/rebar`).\n\n## Guard construction\nFollow the guard-test construction rule in the parent epic `airborne-wellloved-kingfisher`: owner\nmodule exempt, match the constituent conjunction or AST shape named in Approach (or the\ndefinition count where no distinctive atom exists), `# <construct>-ok: <reason>` escape marker,\nand behaviour pinned only by the named existing tests.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_commands/lifecycle_cascade.py` (new), `src/rebar/_commands/claim.py`,\n`src/rebar/_commands/transition.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py`,\n`tests/unit/commands/test_lifecycle_cascade.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: claiming a child of an open parent claims the parent first on both surfaces. Edge: a\nparent already taken by another session raises `ConcurrencyMismatch` with the same exit code as\ntoday. Pinning: `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_claim_transition_parent_cascade.py` and the\ncascade tests from `cranial-sulfur-peafowl`/`paragonite-fruited-minnow` pass unchanged.\n\n## Code-reading corrections (summary; full detail in the ticket comments)\n1. The plan originally named `_cascade_open_parent`, which does not exist anywhere in `src/` or\n   `tests/`. The real helper is `transition._cascade_parent_first`. Corrected throughout.\n2. The cascade fires on THREE edges, not one: `(open→in_progress): open`, `(closed→open): closed`,\n   `(closed→in_progress): closed`. A consolidation built on the one-edge belief would silently\n   drop the reopen and reactivation cascades. `* → closed` must keep NOT cascading.\n3. `reopen` already cascades — it is a thin `transition(id, \"closed\", \"open\")`, so it inherits the\n   `(closed→open)` row. Bug `cranial-sulfur-peafowl` is therefore already fixed; the consolidation\n   must preserve that.\n4. There are THREE walks but only TWO decision copies, which is why the shared module extracts the\n   walk and not the table (see Approach).\n5. No test patches any cascade symbol by name and no string/`getattr` reference exists, so the\n   extraction is free to rename. The only couplings are lazy function-body imports and the\n   load-bearing `cascade=False` kwarg used by the replay seam at `_io/import_ndjson.py:347`.\n\n`despotic-prime-reindeer` (`bb73-97de-eeea-4899`) is `in_progress` with its work already merged as\nGerrit 2044, not an open bug as the plan first said.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `grep -rnE \"^_CASCADING_EDGES\" src/rebar` returns exactly one definition (`transition.py:415`); checked by the grep and the guard test. (The originally-written pattern `_CASCADING_EDGES\\s*=` could never match: the definition carries a type annotation between the name and the `=`, and `\\s` is not basic-regex anyway.)\n- [x] Every edge in the table is exercised by the same test for both `claim` and `transition`; checked by a parametrised test over the table.\n- [x] Pinning suites pass unchanged; checked by `pytest`.\n- [x] The inbound reconcile cascade that landed in Gerrit 2044 routes through the shared implementation, or the leaf records why it stays separate; checked by reading `apply_inbound_events.py` and the guard test.\n- [x] The leaf states whether `reopen` uses the consolidated cascade; checked by the description and, if it does, by a test.\n- [x] All THREE cascading edges keep working after the extraction; checked by the 32 tests in `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_claim_transition_parent_cascade.py` passing unchanged.\n- [x] The inbound cascade added by Gerrit 2044 keeps its own write primitive and its ordering guarantee; checked by `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_inbound_status_cascade.py` passing unchanged.\n- [x] `* -> closed` still does NOT cascade; checked by `test_close_does_not_cascade_to_parent`.\n- [x] The `cascade=False` replay suppression still works; checked by the two `*_cascade_false_suppresses_cascade` tests and `_io/import_ndjson.py`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/lifecycle_cascade.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/claim.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"tests/unit/commands/test_lifecycle_cascade.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a"],["relates_to","0446-4278-b7df-438d"],["relates_to","3939-c860-0637-46af"],["relates_to","5b13-b5a5-6b88-4772"],["relates_to","bb73-97de-eeea-4899"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","parent_status_uuid":"9c8adc80-536e-419d-b887-e494b42131bc","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["consolidation","janitor","fortnight-review"],"ticket_id":"4329-4761-6e3d-41d7","ticket_type":"story","title":"One parent-first cascade shared by claim and transition","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7137fb57-46dc-4c63-a14d-07a77cf3f68c","5ab71f14-1baf-4445-aa9a-38b389f0fbcb","af73090f-65af-4bcd-a4f6-79cd471f7134","9c8adc80-536e-419d-b887-e494b42131bc","f1785e87-5f94-4068-b459-811c2fecd51c","3ff64078-7ef0-4825-9ea5-c417990cbde2","de545f09-fa21-4886-affb-1daf5c02b51a","ea45bb57-c45f-4b36-bb9a-b91c3d12fd6c","6b86c0bf-2be2-457d-9464-2eaf08aee984","d13ec437-0f21-48d0-91ce-b6a3c33558c8","6b26f6e9-e6e5-4eec-b49b-9e332673b77f","fd458a94-380b-4bc6-8639-d90c870dcba4","ad08b929-5645-4136-bf76-19bfe1359a8e","4842a04d-30f0-45a6-b4e2-96568a816641"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787376261692816002,"uuid":"05735278-3a9d-41c5-b398-c8cea6c91044"}